  "body": "An audit for redundant files and dead code. It found **less dead code than expected** — and one real bug.\n\n### The bug\n`deploy-tls` was in `.PHONY` but had **no target body** — the Makefile rewrite in the portability work dropped it. `make deploy-tls` printed \"Nothing to be done\" and **exited zero**, silently succeeding while deploying nothing, and `app/k8s-tls/` was orphaned despite ADR-0007 documenting the command.\n\nRestored and rewritten for the current approach: temp render with digest, cert ARN and FQDN injected from Terraform outputs.\n\nFound by checking every `.PHONY` entry has a body — worth keeping as a habit, since a phantom target is worse than a missing one because it reports success.\n\n### Retired\n`sonar-project.properties` → `optional/jenkins/`. It configured a scanner only the Jenkins pipeline invoked; the Actions pipeline uses tflint, checkov and Trivy. Kept rather than deleted because the Jenkins post-mortem cites it directly.\n\n### Stale references fixed\nAll pointed at files the portability refactor deleted — `backend.tf`, `cluster-addons/README.md`, `.checkov.yml`, and ADR-0007. The ADR got a **Superseded** section rather than an edit, since decision records shouldn't be rewritten; the old amendment stays because the failure modes it documents are still true, just no longer this repo's problem.\n\n### Deliberately not removed\n- **14 informational outputs** — nothing in code reads them, but outputs are the public interface and the consumption guide cites several. \"No programmatic consumer\" ≠ dead.\n- **Five identical `versions.tf`** — Terraform requires each module to declare its own `required_providers`. Structural, not accidental.\n- **Everything under `optional/`** — annotated teaching material; the post-mortems are the point.\n\n### Verified\nfmt, tflint, actionlint and `terraform validate` clean across all three roots; every Makefile target resolves; no references remain to any deleted file.",
